# Keep every file byte-identical between the working copy and any clone.
#
# Rationale: the Phase 7 freeze record (docs/phase7_results_freeze.json) stores a
# SHA-256 for each frozen artifact. Git's default end-of-line conversion on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes the
# bytes and therefore the hash, so a fresh clone failed its own integrity check
# even though the data were identical. Disabling text conversion repo-wide keeps
# the hashes verifiable for anyone who downloads the repository.

* -text
